{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/656937-demon-lores-are-meh","id":656937,"title":"Demon lores are meh","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-08T14:42:52-07:00","id":656937,"title":"Demon lores are meh","content":"So I'm reading through my old Demon book. Love everything about the game, but most of the Lores seem kind of...I dunno, weak, particularly when compared with the Descent abilities (or anything else from oWoD). Any fixes for this? Does the translation guide address it at all? And is there anyone who can tell me I'm way off base and that the Lores are awesome?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/961-chewygranola","name":"ChewyGranola","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T16:00:00-07:00","id":657075,"title":"","content":"And thats why i homebrow it making it more attuned to the Spheres from mage.<br /> <br /> In my setting you have 3 levels of powers<br /> <br /> Apocalyptic Forms<br /> Lores<br /> Natural Eccho.<br /> <br /> First off. like i said before. To me, the lores are an extention of the building blocks of creation, by the same hand you can actually manipulate these more easly (like the mages..and in a way it fits within the mage lores). But the mixing of two or more lores for one effect requieres a Ritual<br /> <br /> The Natural Eccho is something bound to the demon and its creation. Every demon created something, right? so. would be more fitting if he had an attachement to this or an attunement which would allow him to conect and bend these elements easier.<br /> <br /> Example: my demon is Alastor, angel of vengeance. Whenever theres a justified vengeance upon someone or act that deserves the calling of Vengeance, he has a +2 automatically to the full damage against that source that generated the Pain. <br /> <br /> just to give you a couple o' ideas<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T16:23:15-07:00","id":657130,"title":"","content":"Some of the Lores are pretty formidable, in my opinion. Lore of Fundament, for example. First level power lets you manipulate gravity! That is pretty crazy when you think about it. (No Paradox either!)<br /> <br /> A lot of the Lores are less powerful, I agree, but in a way, that makes sense. Elohim were created for particular purposes and roles in creation, and their powers represent those roles. After some time, and during the war, they were able to develop new lores that were more effective for the war. But many of the lores are still based around function rather than power level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2430,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","user":"kalinara","date":". 09-08-2015, 07:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T18:24:40-07:00","id":657252,"title":"","content":"My only issue is the High Torment version of each level. They're inconsistent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1119-primal-flame","name":"Primal Flame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1119_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T07:14:33-07:00","id":657849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChewyGranola</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/656937-demon-lores-are-meh#post656937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I'm reading through my old Demon book. Love everything about the game, but most of the Lores seem kind of...I dunno, weak, particularly when compared with the Descent abilities (or anything else from oWoD). Any fixes for this? Does the translation guide address it at all? And is there anyone who can tell me I'm way off base and that the Lores are awesome?</div> </div> </div> </div>I can happily tell you that the Lores <i>are</i> awesome! BUT, I have to admit they aren't perfect, and you aren't really off-base. The Translation Guide doesn't really adjust power levels that I can tell, aside from tweaking the systems to account for math differences (there is a sidebar that explains how, if not for the tweaks, High-Torment effects would be twice as likely using the NWoD system).<br /> <br /> I'm not familiar enough with Descent to properly expound on how their other powers (Apocalyptic Forms, Immunities, etc.) might compare or make up for any disparity between Lores and Exploits/Embeds.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primal Flame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/656937-demon-lores-are-meh?p=657252#post657252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My only issue is the High Torment version of each level. They're inconsistent.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. I think the real problem with the Lores is the inconsistency between High-Torment effects, as well as power levels at each rank.<br /> <br /> For example, Lore of Light 1 is a really good combat power, capable of dealing ranged damage and blinding. It stands out as being a solid power for such a low rank. Lore of Light 5, however, has a pitiful duration (a few turns) and many weaknesses. In almost any conceivable usage, it lags far behind other rank 5 Lores.<br /> <br /> And now that I'm flipping through the Translation Guide, I notice the NWoD version of Light 1 no longer does damage, but there has been no change to Light 5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />Avatar commissioned from the incomparable Melissa Uran.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/966-redford_blade","name":"Redford_Blade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar966_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T08:36:33-07:00","id":657919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Redford_Blade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/656937-demon-lores-are-meh?p=657849#post657849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And now that I'm flipping through the Translation Guide, I notice the NWoD version of Light 1 no longer does damage, but there has been no change to Light 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would you recommend the Translation Guide, to those in want of a proper system for balancing / house-ruling Demon the Fallen?<br /> <br /> I have nothing against the Descent, by the way, but the Abrahamic mythology is more interesting than the notion of a &quot;God Machine&quot;, meaning I'd buy the Translation Guide for the sole purpose of revisiting DtF rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1119-primal-flame","name":"Primal Flame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1119_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T17:11:30-08:00","id":771896,"title":"","content":"The Lores are awesome, but mostly from a descriptive point of view. They are still too strict in their effects, and full of inconsistencies here and there. I think that a take on them more akin to Mage's Spheres, even if starting from the given Lores instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T18:35:24-08:00","id":776351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/656937-demon-lores-are-meh?p=771896#post771896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Lores are awesome, but mostly from a descriptive point of view. They are still too strict in their effects, and full of inconsistencies here and there. I think that a take on them more akin to Mage's Spheres, even if starting from the given Lores instead.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> ^this<br /> Also if you look at the story, lores work more like spheres than they do in machanics and If you look at the TEN in time of babel it hints that the fallen might have CREATED the mages spheres as a way for humanity to manipulate their god-sparks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T12:12:46-08:00","id":776724,"title":"","content":"I always use the Lore rules on the Howling Void blog. The blog writer IHateAllLife has a cool and simple system for using Lores for spontaneous effects like Spheres. Its stood me and my Fallen player in good stead thus far. check it out","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1919-muadib","name":"muadib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T12:56:21-08:00","id":776754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>muadib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/656937-demon-lores-are-meh?p=776724#post776724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always use the Lore rules on the Howling Void blog. The blog writer IHateAllLife has a cool and simple system for using Lores for spontaneous effects like Spheres. Its stood me and my Fallen player in good stead thus far. check it out</div> </div> </div> </div>Um, you may have pointed in the wrong direction. I just checked it and found nothing about cWOD on the blog.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-30T03:32:21-08:00","id":777081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/656937-demon-lores-are-meh?p=776754#post776754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Um, you may have pointed in the wrong direction. I just checked it and found nothing about cWOD on the blog.</div> </div> </div> </div>Son of a gun, the site is down and gone. What the heck? Sorry about that guys, will check with the owner and see whats going on. I did copy the stuff down onto Word docs for my own games, will see if its ok to share.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1919-muadib","name":"muadib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-30T09:13:26-08:00","id":777181,"title":"","content":"I prefer's Devil's Due system for the Fallen. It's pretty easy to mock up the merged character's from DtF than the Earthbound and possessed of Devil's Due. It's Torment and Power system lends itself well, and is generally more balanced.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-30T22:45:45-08:00","id":777551,"title":"","content":"I just want to take this moment to state my appreciation for the first level of Lore of Light. It's not identical, but it's similar to that flash-power the demons and angels on Supernatural have when ever they raise their palms toward someone. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://twitter.com/mercurial891/status/671580716065497089\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/mercurial891/sta...80716065497089</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","user":"Mercurial","date":". 12-01-2015, 01:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T14:13:01-08:00","id":777912,"title":"","content":"I don't recall demons ever being able to do that on the show. Of course, they're not fallen angels as they are in the game, so the comparison still works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T16:45:20-08:00","id":777972,"title":"","content":"Lilith could, in that last episode when Dean got dragged down by a hellhound. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://powerlisting.wikia.com/wiki/Dark_Light_Manipulation\" target=\"_blank\">http://powerlisting.wikia.com/wiki/D...t_Manipulation</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T13:16:44-08:00","id":778550,"title":"","content":"That's right! She whited out everything when she blew up the police station in &quot;Jus in Bello&quot; as well, didn't she?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T14:49:46-08:00","id":778608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/656937-demon-lores-are-meh?p=778550#post778550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's right! She whited out everything when she blew up the police station in &amp;quot;Jus in Bello&amp;quot; as well, didn't she?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup. But to be fair she was sort of the Bruce Lee of the Fallen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}